---------------------------------------------------------------------------
COPYRIGHT AND SCOPE
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

HyBreDe is a MULTI-AUTHOR work. It began as a group ICT capstone project at
Turku University of Applied Sciences and was afterwards developed further,
independently, by Zoi Theofilakou.

Both copyright lines above are therefore deliberate:

  * The first is the licence and copyright notice carried by the original
    capstone repository. It applies to the collaboratively authored code -
    which includes, among others, Retrieval/retrieval.py, llm/interface.py,
    run_manifest.py, console_utils.py, project_paths.py and the PDF
    acquisition modules. That notice is reproduced here unchanged and is not
    superseded, replaced or narrowed by anything in this repository.

  * The second covers the independent post-capstone work: the evidence
    sufficiency gate, claim-support and citation-identity verification, the
    freeze/provenance controls, the evaluation harness, the current Streamlit
    interface and the public-release sanitization.

Per-file authorship, derived from line-level `git blame` on the original
history, is set out in CONTRIBUTIONS.md. NOTHING HERE RELICENSES
COLLABORATOR-AUTHORED CODE UNDER A SINGLE AUTHOR'S NAME. The original work was
already MIT-licensed, this release stays MIT, and the terms are unchanged; only
the second copyright line has been added, for the material added since.

If you are a capstone collaborator and want your contribution attributed
differently, or removed, that will be acted on request.

WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER

  * Third-party scientific literature, publisher PDFs, extracted full text or
    any other copyrighted corpus material. None is included; see DATA_POLICY.md.
  * The frozen research evidence store / index. Not included.
  * Third-party models, libraries and services (all-MiniLM-L6-v2,
    cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2, ChromaDB, Sentence Transformers,
    OpenAI, Ollama, the Semantic Scholar Graph API). Each remains under its own
    licence and terms.
  * University capstone deliverable documents (e.g. the technical
    documentation report). Not included.

Documentation written for this public release is licensed separately; see
LICENSE-docs.
